If you happen to be playing in Wizard mode (which, if you ask me, is the only   method which allowed me to ascend in 3.0j), you can try this:
(WARNING.  POSSIBLY STUPID SPOILER, BUT THEN AGAIN, WHO KNOWS?)

Make sure you have a pair of gloves on, and then wish for a cockatrice corpse,  so you can use it to turn everything to stone.  Works better than that potion   of paralysis trick for keeping that darn Wizard from annoying you too much,  If you don't have any wishes, try creating the monster, or just go around looking  for a cockatrice.  They don't make good meals, but they make great weapons.     Only problem with this is that it is impossible to preserve cockatrice corpses  without tinning them, and who w

ants to go around bashing Nazguls with a tin of  cockatrice meat?'

This corpse thing works great with gauntlets of power, especially (for 3.0j) in the castle, any room packed with monsters, Vlad's or the Wizard's tower, and    the endgame level.  Especially great on rust monsters -- as long as you hit 'em.

And the best thing about the cockatrice corpse is ... it will work no matter    what alignment you are.

